# Web Push — the VAPID PUBLIC key, and only ever the public half.
#
# Committed deliberately. This is not a secret: Vite compiles it into the JS
# bundle, so it is already served to every visitor, and its whole job is to be
# handed to the browser's PushManager as applicationServerKey. The private half
# lives in exactly two write-only places — the walletlens-push worker's secret
# store and the VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY GitHub secret — and must never appear here.
#
# It is committed rather than left to the environment because leaving it there
# is what broke push: deploy-site.yml passed no VITE_ variables, so every build
# shipped an empty key and enabling notifications failed with "Push isn't
# configured yet (missing key)". A committed default means any build — CI, a
# laptop, a one-off zip — carries a working key. CI still overrides it from the
# secret, since a `env:` entry beats a .env file.
#
# It MUST stay the pair walletlens-push signs with. A browser subscription is
# cryptographically bound to the key that created it, and subscriptionMatchesKey
# drops any subscription made under a different one. Rotating means: set both
# halves on the worker, update this line, rebuild, redeploy.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BMdhWsFzotTYLvKgUl4QFTIxfOuFKUdQhh3dJRjFIuqpAII72QLnbyGZxd0LOP2R2Z3v8XoajpI62fbA2auYxU0
